        "description": "One oblique apparatus view: two side pulleys with axle projections; a cord runs from the left pulley to the central winding drum and onward to the right pulley. Each pulley has two descending cord strands attached to a shallow circular weight/collar region and one lower narrow weight body. Left weight body is offset toward its right side; right weight body toward its left side in perspective. One central winding drum has a crank above and a continuous vertical shaft below, including a small collar/coupling, entering the lid of one calorimeter. The calorimeter has a cylindrical wall, oval lid/rim, a small unlabeled raised lid fitting, and rests on one perspective rectangular/slotted base. Source short wall strokes and drum/base hatching are material shading, not numbered calibration. No letters, arrows, units or numerical readings are present. Modern additions: Unmeasured apparatus geometry and shading regularized; one English identification heading. No hidden blades drawn in this exterior view.",
